// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// E18 runtime-spawner test set piece. Same sealed room as closet-reveal, but
// the closet holds an entity_spawner instead of pre-placed enemies: the plate
// fires spawnFromSpawner to materialize fresh AI enemies at runtime (the path
// the round-1 feet-to-center fix touched). Watch that spawned enemies stand
// on the floor, not sunk into it, and walk out through the doorway.
// Compile: cargo run -p postretro-level-compiler -- content/dev/maps/spawner-test.map -o content/dev/maps/spawner-test.prl
// Run: cargo run -p xtask -- run content/dev/maps/spawner-test.prl
// Sealed room, interior 288 x 256 x 128 units, wall thickness 16, with a
// recessed closet nook carved into the solid east block. The nook interior
// spans x 176 to 272, y 96 to 160, z 0 to 96, entered through a doorway at
// x 176 that the sliding door occludes. The nook and main room form a single
// enclosed interior joined by that internal doorway, so the world hull is
// sealed with no leak. Worldspawn brush order: floor, ceiling, west, east,
// south, north walls, east block south of nook, east block north of nook,
// closet back wall, closet lintel. Every brush is an axis-aligned box wound
// normal-inward, so there are no degenerate duplicate-point faces.
// NOTE: keep map comments free of braces and quotes; the .map parser does not
// fully strip // comments and those characters break the parse.
